{
  "_comment": [
    "Hoodrich gang turf overlay, drawn on the map as shaded blocks.",
    "",
    "A zone like DAVIS is enormous and shading all of it swallows half the south side, so",
    "each gang's turf is described here as a handful of rectangles over the blocks they",
    "actually run, not as one circle per zone.",
    "",
    "gang    id from gangs.json",
    "zone    GET_NAME_OF_ZONE code this block sits in; used for ownership and capture",
    "name    what the block is called on screen",
    "x, y    centre of the rectangle in world coordinates",
    "w, h    size in metres, w across the rotation, h along it",
    "rot     rotation in degrees, clockwise from north. Los Santos streets run about 30",
    "        degrees off north, so most city blocks use 30 and rural turf uses 0.",
    "",
    "These are placed by eye and are meant to be tuned in game: open the wheel, Turf >",
    "Edit blocks, and walk the rectangle onto the streets you want. Saving writes to",
    "Documents\\Hoodrich\\turf.json, which overrides this file and survives reinstalling.",
    "",
    "A gang turf zone with no rectangle here falls back to a circle the size of the zone."
  ],
